{"name":"Urban Exploration","hex":"#89776e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"urban exploration","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The exploration of man-made, particularly urban, environments; such exploration in places which are not normally accessible due to prohibited access or abandonment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urban_exploration"}],"entries":[{"title":"Urban exploration","blocks":[{"text":"Urban exploration is the exploration of manmade structures, usually abandoned ruins or hidden components of the built environment. Photography and historical documentation are heavily featured in the hobby, generally involving trespassing onto private property."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Thomas_Bresson_-_Fort_du_Salbert-8_%28by%29.JPG/330px-Thomas_Bresson_-_Fort_du_Salbert-8_%28by%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_exploration"},{"title":"Exploration","blocks":[{"text":"Exploration is the process of exploring, an activity which has some expectation of discovery. Organised exploration is largely a human activity, but exploratory activity is common to most organisms capable of directed locomotion and the ability to learn, and has been described in, amongst others, social insects foraging behaviour, where feedback from returning individuals affects the activity of other members of the group."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exploration"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Urban_Explorer_in_the_entrance_of_technical_gallery.jpg/500px-Urban_Explorer_in_the_entrance_of_technical_gallery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Urban_Explorer_in_the_entrance_of_technical_gallery.jpg/500px-Urban_Explorer_in_the_entrance_of_technical_gallery.jpg?utm